WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.680
- I was in high school and
we were looking at a film

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.840
and it was looking at the degradation

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.340
of homelessness and disparity.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.440
And I said, wow, man, those
people are really fucked up.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.023
I'll never end up like that.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.180
And about two years ago,

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.763
I was on one of the back
streets here on Skid Row,

00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:19.413
and it dawned on me what I said.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.670
And I said, I'll be damned.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.770
I became one of those people.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.230
- All right, Norman.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.140
Norman, where'd you grow up?

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.270
Where are you from originally?

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.210
- I'm originally from Detroit, Michigan.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.257
- And tell me about your family.

00:00:37.257 --> 00:00:39.000
You had both parents growing up?

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.330
- No, I had one parent.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.914
Didn't know my father, didn't meet him

00:00:41.914 --> 00:00:44.773
until the day before my 18th birthday.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.173
Came out here,

00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:50.440
grew up in the Country Club
Park district of Los Angeles.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.940
- At what age?

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.893
- 14 months old.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.480
Went to 24th Street School,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.320
had two very smart sisters
that I had to follow behind.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.713
I always liked to read.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.320
Got straight A's in elementary school.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.433
September the 2nd, 1976, devastating.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.370
I watched my mother take her last breath.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.643
She died of a massive cerebral hemorrhage.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.570
My grandmother came from
Detroit to take me back.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:19.460
- You saw this?

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.370
- Yes.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.720
- How old were you?

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.996
- I was 12 years old.

00:01:22.996 --> 00:01:23.980
- 12, Jesus.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:24.813
- 12 years old.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:28.200
- So you went back to Detroit?

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.890
- Yes, went back to Detroit.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.100
To describe my grandmother a little bit,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.040
six foot two and a half,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.500
295 pound Sequoia Indian

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.080
born in Moose Head, Saskatchewan, Canada.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.253
Very strict.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.003
I wouldn't say mean, but very ruly.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.260
When I was 15 years old,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.710
something devastating happened to me.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.330
A family friend molested me,

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:54.540
threw me down and inserted hisself in me.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.883
I never told anybody, never told anybody.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.920
Graduated from high school,
Detroit Northern high school.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.863
Straight A's, most likely to
succeed, and best dressed.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.710
Won the Adlai Stevenson Award

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:12.220
to go to Baylor University.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.330
Graduated in three years

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.520
with a Bachelor's of
Science in computer science.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:20.270
I had before then applied
for the Fritz Kreisler Award.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.623
I won it, went to Michigan.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.750
Graduated magna cum laude,

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.000
and I started working
for Ford Motor Company.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.920
Switched over to General
Dynamics, it was more money.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.040
When I was about 24 and a half, 25,

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.693
I discovered crack cocaine.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.943
My first time, I went and
drew $5,000 out of the bank.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.803
I didn't go back to work and
that started my downfall.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.883
I've put myself in very
precarious situations,

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:59.430
gay men have come up to me and
asked me for sexual favors.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.263
I've done it.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:06.400
I lost my grandmother in
1985, which was another blow.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.360
- And you're not gay.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.693
- No, I'm not gay at all.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.681
Totally, totally straight.

00:03:11.681 --> 00:03:14.200
Nobody's ever inserted themself into me,

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.973
with the exception of
the guy who molested me.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.670
But I've put myself in positions

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.673
to where thank God that I don't have HIV.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.983
You're looking at a
person who's had it all.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.600
Through the course of my addiction,

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.673
I've lost six houses,
one condo, five cars.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.760
My average salary is anywhere

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.033
from 95 to 245,000 dollars a year.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.010
- Now you're living on the street.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.830
- Yeah, and now I'm living on the streets.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.810
My nightly routine usually consists of

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.080
going on the Metrorail to either
Long Beach or Santa Monica

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.410
because they're the longest ones.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:03:59.560
Once they put you off of that,

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.540
then I'll get on the bus.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.640
Either the 33 or the 60 and I'll ride.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.060
- It's safer to ride a
bus or a train than...

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.600
- Yes, yes. Than to be on the streets.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.203
You have so many precarious
situations that happen.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.930
It's a catch-as-catch-can
when you're homeless.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.270
You never know what's going to happen.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:19.473
You never know what the next move is.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.790
So I've been a crack cocaine addict

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.380
for the better part of 32, 33 years.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:27.640
- You have kids?

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.673
- I have four kids.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.493
Ranging from 32 years old to nine.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:38.123
Of course, right now,
they don't hear from me.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.820
I had a phone and I was jonesing,

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.570
and then I sold my phone

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.063
after I spent $253 to get it.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.503
It is what it is.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.010
I've been in recovery before.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.823
I've been in about 55
different treatment centers.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.590
Longest lift in sobriety I've ever had

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.173
was six years, 10 months, and two days.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.600
I blew that because I got cocky,

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.550
I thought I had it.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.890
I haven't been able to
muster up 90 days since,

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:16.303
and that's been about 18, 19 years ago.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.363
Homelessness is systemic.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:27.723
It's something that you
really don't plan on,

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.523
but you quickly learn
how to adapt and survive.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.553
Well, when I was young,
I was 16 years old,

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.140
I was in high school and
we were looking at a film

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.290
and they were looking at the degradation

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.810
