00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.630
I've been to Park Avenue,

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.023
now I'm on a park bench.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:03.763
I've had the riches, now I have rags.

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.133
But it's up to me, choice is mine.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.270
- Have you talked about
these things before?

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.710
- No. No, not really.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.503
People only know about my schooling.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.933
They know about my family.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.963
My last name is Fondren.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:29.823
I'm not even going to
say anything about that,

00:13:29.823 --> 00:13:32.560
I'll just have you look up the last name.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.943
It's a family that dates back to 1218.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.690
It's a family that has a family crest.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:41.733
It's a family that's extremely prominent.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.270
I have not lived up to that billing.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.853
I was bred and coded to do that,

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.400
but for some reason I got
attracted to the street life

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.350
because it was something that
I was always told not to do

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.950
and it seemed like as I'm going to church

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.770
as a young kid with my grandmother

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.860
and as I'm being sequestered

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.380
and have to come in
when the lights are on,

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:10.113
everybody else is having fun.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.870
Thank God for my
grandmother, she warned me.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.993
Everything she ever told me has come true.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.090
She said, if you get with those people,

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.690
you're going to be
exactly like those people

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:27.550
and the only way you're
going to go is down.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.000
And that's what has happened.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:32.880
- Have you lost touch with
all your friends and family

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:33.713
and things like that?

00:14:33.713 --> 00:14:35.970
- My immediate friends, yes.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:38.890
They don't really want
to be bothered anymore

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.100
because they know that I'm going to lie

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.380
about something to get some money.

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:43.293
My family,

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:48.510
my oldest sister understands a little bit.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:49.903
My middle sister,

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.640
we don't have the
relationship we used to have

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.790
based on the fact that
I stole her wedding ring

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:56.890
and her husband's wedding ring

00:14:56.890 --> 00:15:01.290
after she sent for me to come
out here in the first place.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.593
How did I repay her?

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.130
Just like I repaid everybody else.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.980
Just like I've done everybody else.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:07.813
Fuck them.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.633
When the disease says go, I go.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.380
- What do you think the
solution is to your situation?

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:19.830
What would help you if you were

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.270
ready to change and wanted to?

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.850
What do you think would be the first step?

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:25.960
- Well, I think the first step
is being honest with myself

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:29.213
and understanding that
I do have an addiction.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.473
I do have a disease.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.010
Understanding that it's
more powerful than I am.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.910
I do in some respects, but
I don't respect that shit.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:40.810
I don't give a fuck.

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:43.600
If I could take a hit right now, I would.

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:44.640
Do I want one right now?

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.090
You damn right, I do.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.210
Because that's just how it is.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.280
But I gotta be honest within myself

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:55.280
and be willing to stop
and be willing to change.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.140
Am I afraid of that change?

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.900
Yes, I do have fear of the unknown.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.806
I've come to grips with that.

00:16:00.806 --> 00:16:03.060
If I can't see it, taste it, and feel it,

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.980
I ain't fucking with it.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.310
But yet again, I act on faith.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:09.580
If they say faith is the
substance of things hoped for

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:11.340
and the evidence of things not seen,

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.373
a friend comes around the
corner, his eyes are wide.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:17.610
He said, Hey man, they got some bomb.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.650
Now, it's a substance of things hoped for,

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:22.010
so I'm hoping to get like him.

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:23.220
The evidence of things not seen,

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:25.150
I didn't see the crack,

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.810
but I went and I acted in faith.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.550
So faith works in various ways,

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.450
you gotta really look at that.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:32.870
I just gotta be willing to change.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:35.940
I gotta be willing to want
to stop getting high, period.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:38.570
It's just not crack,
I don't need anything.

00:16:38.570 --> 00:16:41.260
If I drink a beer, I'm
gonna smoke some rocks.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:43.760
If I smoke some weed, I'm
going to smoke some rocks.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.290
If I think about smoking some rocks,

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:46.890
I'm going to smoke some rocks.

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:48.110
So I gotta be honest with myself

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.940
and I gotta be willing inside, in here,

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:52.460
to say, Hey Norman, enough is enough.

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:55.010
You would think at 56 years
old that I would learn.

00:16:58.010 --> 00:16:59.060
Doesn't look like it.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:03.070
- What's the most important
thing you've learned

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:04.820
from your years on the street?

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:05.670
- How to survive.

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:09.683
It's a bitch being hungry.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.853
Hunger is something that's
very, very fucked up.

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:18.980
It doesn't get to the depths
of the third world countries

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:21.880
where people are starving,
starving, but I've been hungry.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:26.220
I've ran out of Ralph's with
a fully cooked slab of ribs,

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:28.500
baby back ribs, chicken.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.220
I went in 99 cents stores

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:34.253
and ditched a security guard
and stolen candy just to eat.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.313
I've eaten out of the garbage can.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.620
I've seen a drink at a bus stop

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.350
and I've looked around and I've drank it

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.450
because I was thirsty.

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.730
But two days earlier, I just
had four, five hundred dollars.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:56.633
So I've learned how to
survive, most importantly.

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.053
- What regrets do you have?

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:06.470
- My regret is July the 19th, 1986.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.080
That's when I took my first hit.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:15.133
I regret doing that.

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.490
I've often looked back and said,

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:21.113
if I would've never done that,

00:18:22.768 --> 00:18:24.913
but if if was a fifth, we'd all be drunk,

00:18:26.702 --> 00:18:28.002
the cliche's go on and on,

00:18:29.314 --> 00:18:31.200
but if I would have never taken that,

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:32.433
where would I be now?

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:37.230
At that time, I was working
for General Dynamics.

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:42.230
I was 23 and a half, 24,
making $74,000 a year.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.100
Had one of the best apartments

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:50.880
that you could see in
Detroit, the Jeffersonian.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:53.630
That's where I stayed,
right down on Jefferson.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:54.850
I look over my balcony,

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:57.500
I'm looking at Windsor,
Canada and the Detroit River.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:01.350
Now, I'm looking at
rats, I'm smelling piss,

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.460
and I'm stepping over people,

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:06.930
and struggling every day to survive.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.390
I'm struggling every day to eat,

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.500
I'm struggling every day
to smoke a cigarette,

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.323
I'm struggling every day to get a hit.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:17.533
My regret is July 19th, 1986.

00:19:19.821 --> 00:19:21.363
- Do you see any signs that

00:19:21.363 --> 00:19:23.093
you're getting close to making a change?

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:25.353
- I don't know.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.160
I was talking to my buddy and
he looked at me this morning,

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:31.510
he said, man, what's wrong?

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:35.080
I said, man, I'm really
getting tired of this.

00:19:37.551 --> 00:19:40.620
He's like, Norm, I've
known you for a long time.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:42.460
He said, man, you smart,
you can come out of it.

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:45.310
I said it ain't got a damn
thing to do with intelligence,

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:49.263
has everything to do with wherewithal.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:55.183
I think God and I have a problem.

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:00.883
Yeah, cause I'm a mama's boy.

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:07.293
It always happens when
I talk about my mom,

00:20:09.427 --> 00:20:13.737
because that was fucked up
that I had to watch that.

00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:18.153
I always think about her.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.027
She was lighter, way lighter than me

00:20:21.027 --> 00:20:22.313
and I look just like her.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:28.073
And a lot of times I think
she's really not proud of me.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:34.760
So that's it, we're gonna do our best.

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:35.593
- All right, Norm.

00:20:35.593 --> 00:20:36.440
Well, good luck, man.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.273
- Okay.

00:20:37.273 --> 00:20:38.410
- Great speaking with you.

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:43.140
- Wow. That's the first
time I did that one.

